al\">Vampires</span></td> </tr> </table></div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T19:13:52-07:00","id":1519694,"title":"","content":"A very niche one: The active affect of Vigor that boosts damage only works when using Strength based attack rolls, that way a Dexterity based attack roll can\u2019t benefit from Praestania and Vigor","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23575-mrmonsterguy18","name":"MrMonsterGuy18","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-06T07:13:26-07:00","id":1519951,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking to allow Resilience to be added against mental disciplines. Kind of what Masquerade V5 does. But still have to better evalaute it. I find the mental disciplines mechanic too drifted in favor of the attacker. I like the idea that also elders have to be worried about younger (aka lower BP) kindreds, but as of yet it's way too much shifted thowards the user imho.<br /> <br /> Also I'm thinking how to rework a bit Auspex as it's literally &quot;almost&quot; unnoticeable and with very few way to resist it. I'm thinking to make its utilization a bit more obvious (e.g.: eyes whitening, etc) so that if you are aware of the power and you can see the user, you should be able to guess what he's doing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 08-07-2023, 03:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-08T19:24:03-07:00","id":1520166,"title":"","content":"For myself, Dampier are run as ghoul family(+) to play up their mixed heritage rather than the current canon version. Not that the official version is bad, just not the tropes I'm looking for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-09T09:01:59-07:00","id":1520207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1518877-what-are-your-vampire-house-rules?p=1519951#post1519951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm thinking to allow Resilience to be added against mental disciplines. Kind of what Masquerade V5 does. But still have to better evalaute it. I find the mental disciplines mechanic too drifted in favor of the attacker. I like the idea that also elders have to be worried about younger (aka lower BP) kindreds, but as of yet it's way too much shifted thowards the user imho.</div> </div> </div> </div>How about simply making it a Devotion as a compromise?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-09T10:00:18-07:00","id":1520217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1518877-what-are-your-vampire-house-rules?p=1520207#post1520207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How about simply making it a Devotion as a compromise?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>A devotion is something you have to develop, learnt specifically for this purpose. I see the mental disciplines mechanic a bit broken by raw, so I'd like a way accessibile to everyone to mitigate it. I'm not a fan of devotions shared by all the kindred. To me devotions are supposed to characterize better a vampire. On the other end Resilience is a common discipline who most ancillae or elders may have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-12T20:01:43-07:00","id":1520497,"title":"","content":"Compiled my list of house rules for Vampire: The Requiem 2e!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/17SsOsKpfdANVZscFHSO_afTx-gD3h0iX3p5q07V4u50/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/17SsOsKpfdANVZscFHSO_afTx-gD3h0iX3p5q07V4u50/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/17SsOsKpfdANVZscFHSO_afTx-gD3h0iX3p5q07V4u50/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/17SsOsKpfdANVZscFHSO_afTx-gD3h0iX3p5q07V4u50/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Proud creator of <b><a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/420206/Curiouser-and-Curiouser-Bargains\" target=\"_blank\">Curiouser and Curiouser Bargains</a></b>, a collection of 30+ Homebrew Contracts and 10+ Entitlements on the STV!<br /> My <b><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1GFE19F9st7dhGh9zv_hEQyOSm80Xp7dQwmvFg2SAXJY/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules</a></b> for Changeling!<br /> My <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/17SsOsKpfdANVZscFHSO_afTx-gD3h0iX3p5q07V4u50/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><b>House Rules</b></a> for Vampire!<br /> My <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1kR6ASTLjaEDwl3zgANnkRrbk0-s2bvw40uXwS-q15O0/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><b>House Rules</b></a> for Geist!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27667-super-vlad","name":"Super Vlad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27667_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-13T03:06:38-07:00","id":1520508,"title":"","content":"Others house rules we have already adopted for long time, and seems they work just fine are:<br /> <br /> <b><u>Jumps</u></b>: For a jump done without stress or pressure there's no roll, it is automatically considered that the dice pool get half of the successes (rounded down or up depending if you want a more action based play style ). A stressful situation comes with a normal roll (e.g.: During a chase, with time pressure, jumping from buildings when not used to it by the play stile of the character, etc)<ul><li><u><i>Vertical Jump</i></u>: [(Strength + Vigor + Athletics) successes/3]<i>(Vigor + 1)</i> in meters</li> <li><i><u>Horizontal Jump</u>:</i> [(Strength + Vigor + Athletics) successes](Vigor + 1) in meters</li> <li><i><u>Horizontal Jump with run-up</u></i>: [[(Strength + Vigor + Athletics) Successes] + Size] *(Vigor + 1) in meters.</li> </ul>This mechanic was worked around Humans. It seems to provide reliable output quite close to real human's jump distances. Vigor simply multiplies the human's output, obtained putting Vigor 0 into the formulas. In fact considering a top athlete, let's say Strength 4, athletic 5 (or any combination with Merits which may compensate lower attributes), we get a 9 meters broad run jump, or 1.2 meters vertical (meaning from floor to feet). Same way for an average amateur athlete: strength 2, athletic 3 we get: 7 meters broad and 66 cm vertical.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Falling and Landing</u></b>:<br /> <br /> We believe that the falling damage is, by raw, way too low leading to underestimate the threat of a possible fall.<br /> A controlled fall (landing on feet) does not cause damage if the individual can vertically jump a distance equal to the fall - 1 meter. For example, with Vigor, one might be able to jump vertically several tens of meters, and in this case, landing after such a jump or letting oneself fall from an equivalent height does not cause damage. This is because the character has the necessary strength to cushion the impact with their legs. Otherwise, one sustains impact damage for every 3 meters beyond the aforementioned height, up to a maximum of 30 meters. At this height, mortal creatures suffer a maximum of 10 lethal damages, while vampires always sustain impact damage. If one doesn't land in a controlled manner (thus on their back or not on their legs), the damage is doubled. It is possible to try to limit the damages in a controlled fall, with a roll on dexterity+athletics. In a controlled fall, in fact, the character might be able to divert the force of the impact, rolling effectively at the moment of impact. Every success achieved on this roll reduces the damage by one. This maneuver is not possible for uncontrolled falls, but it is always possible, with a roll on dexterity+athletics with appropriate penalties, to try to grasp onto some handhold.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Animalism 3 (attacking Swarm)</u></b>:<br /> <br /> This is taken from Demon the Descent Swarm Mechanic and applied to Summoning the Hunts (Bigger animals coming together with the swarm may be handled separately or adding damages as appropriate.<br /> Using Summoning the Hunts (Animalism 3) to summon a flock of birds or rats or both can be well represented by the swarm rules. A flock of crows or a swarm of rats or both (numerous enough to be considered a swarm) which has been ordered to attack one or more targets, means for those within the swarm:<ul><li>The swarm has a radius in meters equal to twice the successes on the roll.</li> <li>The swarm inflicts 1 impact damage on all those inside and can condense. Each time its radius is halved, it adds 1 impact damage. Example: An 8-meter swarm deals 1 impact damage to everyone and, if it concentrates becoming 4 meters in radius, it deals 2 impact damages; if it concentrates further with a 2-meter radius, it deals 3 impact damages and, focusing further to a one-meter radius (1 target), it deals 4. Alternatively, it's simpler to have the damage increase by 1 each turn starting from 0 up to the successes obtained on the roll, with a maximum of 4 damages per turn.</li> <li>Armor is ineffective unless it covers the entire body, and even then, its rating is halved.</li> <li>Penalties to all rolls equal to -2 due to distraction.</li> <li>The swarm cannot be attacked with fists, clubs, or knives, only area attacks are effective. Every damage inflicted by one of these sources halves the radius; when the radius falls below one meter, the swarm disperses.</li> </ul>\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 08-13-2023, 06:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-19T22:34:01-07:00","id":1524311,"title":"","content":"Sorry for slight necro but I like this thread.<br /> <br /> I have a few that I use.<br /> <br /> Blood potency blood pool goes up by 5 per dot of potency, and blood spent goes up 1 per dot. So, blood potency 1 would have 15 blood pool and 1 bp per turn limit. While blood potency 10 would have a blood pool of 60 and 10 blood per turn. This makes the peak a little lower but makes the lower-level vampires still have a good blood pool, it is also easy to track.<br /> <br /> <br /> Willpower costs for disciplines can be overcome by giving the discipline 3 times the willpower required in vitae. This does not change per turn maximum blood expenditure though so you often must charge up this ability at lower blood potency.<br /> <br /> <br /> I reimplement half bashing to vampires as every other edition has it including 5e. Let humans cower when they empty an entire magazine into you, you are a monster something that should eat most bullets like candy.<br /> <br /> <br /> Banes are banes any bane that deals damage gives at least lethal damage some like uninvited give aggravated.<br /> <br /> <br /> I change defense to the higher of dexterity or wits and cut athletics from the roll. I have heard the argument that it is attribute plus skill for offense and defense, but it really isn't equal at all.<br /> <br /> It is rolled attribute plus skill versus static attribute plus skill which gives defense a very definitive advantage.<br /> <br /> As a compromise I allow the higher of wits or dex to be used and allow willpower to add 3 defense instead of 2, I have only tested this in a few games so far but it seems to work. Dodge is unchanged since you are giving up an action, and celerity still raises defense.<br /> <br /> <br /> In the largest break away I rule the embrace fully refreshes willpower instead of taking one away, but it still lowers humanity. The beast wants you to give in and spread the curse and it makes doing so feel right. The beast is corruptive and tempting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27607-bloodyrelight","name":"BloodyRelight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27607_2.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-26T15:29:26-07:00","id":1524552,"title":"","content":"If we ever go back to playing the series anytime. We plan on doing away with the blurred reflection and keep the 1st edition clan weaknesses and keeping the virtue and vice system","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-26T17:01:41-07:00","id":1524556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1518877-what-are-your-vampire-house-rules?p=1524552#post1524552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we ever go back to playing the series anytime. We plan on doing away with the blurred reflection and keep the 1st edition clan weaknesses and keeping the virtue and vice system</div> </div> </div> </div>Truth be told, i have this propensity for having the weaknesses from multiple editions within the same clan, as a hook to tinker with the idea of atavisms of undeath and multiple strains of a lineage, with the Hollow Mekhet and the Grettir as some of the possibly most notable cases.<br /> <br /> Plus some cases of &quot;one of these things is not really like the others&quot; with Julii mislabeled as Ventrue (or Gangrel), Akhud or Jiangshi as Mekhet and so on, for some bit of spam in the works and paranoia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-26-2023, 08:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-28T02:05:11-07:00","id":1524626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1518877-what-are-your-vampire-house-rules?p=1524552#post1524552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we ever go back to playing the series anytime. We plan on doing away with the blurred reflection and keep the 1st edition clan weaknesses and keeping the virtue and vice system</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome, I was always more fond of Virtue and Vice as well. I used a simple pdf editor to edit one of MR Gones 10 dot sheets for using it. I didn't want to trouble him since he already made so many sheets already.<br /> <br /> Here it is if you want it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1FapU6RcyZ_HBWGnomZgLtTuwO14avpIf/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1FapU6RcyZ_HBWGnomZgLtTuwO14avpIf/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1FapU6RcyZ_HBWGnomZgLtTuwO14avpIf/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://drive.google.com/file/d/1FapU6RcyZ_HBWGnomZgLtTuwO14avpIf/view?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27607-bloodyrelight","name":"BloodyRelight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27607_2.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-28T09:10:51-07:00","id":1524640,"title":"","content":"Here are my house rules. For context, I use 1e, so no touchstones, conditions, tilts, or any of that will be accounted for.<br /> <br /> 1. The Fog of Ages is very much still a thing as it's still 1e<br /> <br /> 2. Predator's Taint is not a thing. Vampires do have a &quot;sixth sense&quot; where they can figure out who is Kindred and who is not but it doesn't provoke much of a reaction on its own.<br /> <br /> 3. Blood Potency is a bit different. You can still feed on animals up until BP 5 now and you can still feed on humans all the way to BP 10 but once you hit BP 8, you have to drink twice as much blood from humans to get the same amount of sustenance. Methuselahs retain their Blood Potency even as they slumber but the Fog of Ages is still a thing for them and slumbering long enough can reduce a lot of the feeding restrictions for them despite their high Blood Potency.<br /> <br /> 4. The whole &quot;emotional deadness&quot; fluff from the 1e corebook is gone completely. Even 1e dropped it early on and there's no real way to keep it going in a game anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-28T11:20:21-07:00","id":1524649,"title":"","content":"I like using Predator Taint more like something out of the old Highlander films Matt myself and I see that you done the same thing. In regards to Fog of the Ages we didn't modify it much and viewed it as they get older they would have harder and harder time trying to recall there early nights and things being hazy and going into torpor depending on how it happened might clear up the cobwebs so to speak.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-28T20:09:47-07:00","id":1524673,"title":"","content":"To create a new Vampire, you permanently lose a Blood-Potency Point: you give it to the fledgling. And a BP 5+ can drink from werewolves as the supernatural count as, &quot;Vampire&quot;, for drinking blood (WW-Blood is just as potent with the, &quot;Side-effects&quot;).<br /> <br /> And Dragons have to spend a point of Willpower every time they use their breath-weapon (yeah, you don't want to play my Vamp-games).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-30T16:00:19-07:00","id":1524775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1518877-what-are-your-vampire-house-rules?p=1524649#post1524649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like using Predator Taint more like something out of the old Highlander films Matt myself and I see that you done the same thing. In regards to Fog of the Ages we didn't modify it much and viewed it as they get older they would have harder and harder time trying to recall there early nights and things being hazy and going into torpor depending on how it happened might clear up the cobwebs so to speak.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like NWoD Predator's Taint. For some reason, I always thought, each Vampire-clan had it's own independent creator and over the millennium, that all infused with each other's blood, causing the Taint. As for the Fog of the Ages: I always liked the Memory-virtue from OWoD's Mummy 2nd, and worked that into any ancient-vampire I played. Sure, my character might have had a high-potence or celerity, but, I forgot about it over the ages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}